def legal(path,title,subtitle,summary,sections):
 toc=''.join(f'<a href="#{i}">{n+1:02d}. {t}</a>' for n,(i,t,c) in enumerate(sections))
 content=''.join(f'<section id="{i}"><h2>{n+1}. {t}</h2>{c}</section>' for n,(i,t,c) in enumerate(sections))
 page(path,title,subtitle,f'<div class="wrap subhero"><span class="eyebrow">CLEAR EXPECTATIONS. THOUGHTFUL CARE.</span><h1>{title}</h1><p>{subtitle}</p><p class="draft">Proposed update · September 26, 2026 · Preview draft, not yet effective</p></div><div class="wrap legal-layout"><aside class="legal-toc" aria-label="Page contents"><strong>ON THIS PAGE</strong>{toc}</aside><article class="legal-content"><div class="callout"><p><strong>The short version</strong></p><p>{summary}</p></div>{content}</article></div>')
terms=[
('agreement','The agreement', '''<p>These Terms of Service govern the Embryly application, website, meal catalog, articles, illustrations, and related services (the Service). The Service is operated by Benekan Technologies LLC (Embryly, we, us). Our contact is <a href="mailto:info@benekan.com">info@benekan.com</a>. Once these proposed terms are published with an effective date, your acceptance of them or use of the Service as permitted by applicable law forms an agreement with us. If you do not agree, do not use the Service.</p><p>Our <a href="privacy-policy.html">Privacy Policy</a> explains personal data processing. Accepting these Terms does not replace any separate consent required for sensitive data, optional analytics, or marketing. A summary or headline does not replace the detailed terms. Mandatory consumer and privacy rights always prevail.</p>'''),
('wellness','General wellness, not medical care', '''<p>Embryly offers AI assisted food information, catalog based meal suggestions, and personal tracking. It is not a medical device and is not intended to diagnose, monitor, predict, treat, cure, or prevent disease, assess fetal wellbeing, or direct clinical decisions. It does not provide a clinical nutrition service or establish a relationship with a doctor, midwife, or dietitian. We do not claim regulatory clearance or approval for medical use.</p><p>Consult a qualified medical professional about your individual pregnancy, food choices, supplements, allergies, medications, weight, hydration, and health conditions. Do not change a prescribed diet or treatment, or delay professional care, because of the Service. Guidance for gestational diabetes, anemia, celiac disease, high blood pressure, eating disorders, and other conditions must come from your care team. The Service cannot assess an emergency. Contact emergency services when urgent help is needed.</p>'''),
('ai','AI outputs, safety labels, and accuracy', '''<p><strong>No independently validated overall accuracy percentage has been established for Embryly.</strong> A model’s confidence value, food score, or demonstration result is not a measured probability that a food is safe for you. We do not promise 90%, 100%, or any other numerical accuracy rate. If a legacy screen shows “up to 90%,” it must not be treated as clinical validation or a safety guarantee.</p><p>AI may misidentify a dish, ingredient, brand, serving size, cooking method, or nutrient amount. It can generate plausible statements that are wrong, incomplete, inconsistent, or outdated. Barcode records can be missing or refer to a different formulation or country. A photo cannot verify pasteurization, internal cooking temperature, storage history, allergens, cross contact, contamination, freshness, or a recall.</p><p>Labels such as Safe, Caution, or Avoid are informational categories, not certification that an actual food is free from risk. Check packaging, preparation, storage, manufacturer information, current official guidance, and your clinician’s instructions. If information conflicts or is missing, do not rely on an app label to resolve the uncertainty.</p>'''),
('meals','Meal matching and nutritional estimates', '''<p>Our recommendations select and rank entries in a prepared catalog using information such as pregnancy week, saved ingredient avoidances, dietary and cultural preferences, and recent meal suggestions. AI assists with parts of our content creation and scan analysis; the daily catalog matcher is not a clinician and does not perform a complete nutritional assessment.</p><p>Breakfast, lunch, and dinner options are alternative meal ideas, not an instruction to eat every displayed dish or a guarantee of complete daily nutrition. Portions, preparation times, calories, and nutrients are estimates. Ingredient substitutions, brands, cooking losses, and serving sizes affect the result. Catalog recipes have undergone automated editorial checks but are not all kitchen tested or independently clinically approved.</p><p>Preferences and allergy tags help filter suggestions but cannot guarantee allergen absence or prevent cross contact. Halal and kosher preferences may surface plant based ideas; certification, sourcing, utensils, and preparation still require your own checks. A lower carbohydrate preference is a relative ranking preference, not a prescribed low carbohydrate diet. Some combinations of restrictions may have limited or no suitable matches. We will not represent availability as proof of suitability.</p>'''),
('images','Baby illustrations and food images', '''<p>Baby and fetus visuals are artistic, AI assisted illustrations organized by pregnancy week, not ultrasound images, diagnostic images, or a depiction of your own baby. Anatomy, proportions, skin appearance, posture, and developmental details may be simplified or inaccurate. They are not to scale. Real pregnancies vary, and a displayed week does not establish gestational age, viability, growth, health, or a due date.</p><p>Food images can be generated or illustrative. Appearance does not prove ingredients, portion size, doneness, safety, certification, or nutritional composition. Follow the written ingredient list and preparation guidance, then verify the actual food. Promotional app screens use fictional sample entries; they do not show patient records, measured outcomes, or testimonials.</p>'''),
('sources','Sources and changing information', '''<p>The catalog’s source records reference public guidance from CDC, FoodSafety.gov, FDA/EPA, and the NHS, and nutrient data from USDA FoodData Central, including SR Legacy. Barcode lookups use Open Food Facts, a community maintained database. Our <a href="sources.html">Sources & Accuracy page</a> links to those references and explains their roles.</p><p>These organizations do not sponsor, endorse, or certify Embryly. Referencing a source does not mean every AI sentence or catalog entry has been checked against it. Scan responses are not guaranteed to retrieve current guidance or live recall information. Recommendations differ by jurisdiction and change over time. Follow guidance applicable where you live and seek professional advice for conflicts or individual circumstances.</p>'''),
('eligibility','Eligibility and your account', '''<p>The Service is intended for adults aged 18 or older who can enter a binding agreement. Provide accurate account information and keep your pregnancy dates and preferences current. Protect your credentials and notify us of suspected unauthorized use. You are responsible for activity you authorize, but this does not remove rights relating to fraud or security failures for which the law makes us responsible.</p><p>Do not share another person’s health information without their permission. We may proportionately restrict access for security, misuse, legal obligations, or material violations of these Terms, with notice and an opportunity to resolve the issue where practical and legally appropriate.</p>'''),
('subscriptions','Subscriptions, renewals, and refunds', '''<p>Features may require a subscription. The purchase screen identifies the applicable price, currency, billing period, tax treatment, trial eligibility, and renewal terms. Website preview prices do not override the store’s offer. A weekly and an annual plan are separate recurring subscriptions, not a promise of lifetime access.</p><p>Apple handles App Store billing. Subscriptions normally renew until canceled through your Apple account. A trial, if expressly offered, may convert to a paid subscription under the terms shown when you enroll. Cancel before the applicable renewal or trial deadline. Deleting Embryly, deactivating your account, or contacting our support does not itself cancel an Apple subscription.</p><p>You can <a href="https://support.apple.com/118428">manage or cancel an Apple subscription</a> and <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com/">request a refund through Apple</a>. Refund and withdrawal rights required by your local law remain available. We do not apply a blanket “no refunds” rule to override those rights. Material price or service changes will be notified as required; store rules also apply.</p>'''),
('content','Your content and permission to process it', '''<p>You retain rights in the photos, notes, and other content you submit. You give us a limited, nonexclusive permission to host, transmit, process, and display it as reasonably necessary to provide the requested features, support, and security, subject to the Privacy Policy. This is not an unrestricted license to sell your health data or use your photos in advertising. Any additional use requiring consent needs that separate consent.</p><p>You must have the right to submit content. Keep faces, identity documents, prescription labels, and unrelated personal information out of food photos. AI and infrastructure providers may process content as explained in the Privacy Policy. Our handling of content after a deletion request is subject to applicable law and the retention limitations described there.</p>'''),
('conduct','Permitted use and intellectual property', '''<p>You receive a personal, limited, nontransferable license to use the Service for lawful purposes. Do not access other users’ data, bypass security or usage controls, introduce malware, harass others, submit illegal content, or copy and commercially redistribute the catalog without permission. Restrictions do not override rights that applicable law expressly protects, including lawful interoperability or security research.</p><p>Embryly’s branding, software, and original design are owned by us or licensed to us. Third party datasets, images, and content remain subject to their own rights and licenses. AI output may not be unique or eligible for exclusive ownership; we do not promise that it is. Source attribution does not give you ownership of the source.</p>'''),
('availability','Availability and third party services', '''<p>The Service depends on internet access, device support, app stores, hosting, AI providers, and third party data. Features, content, and availability may change. We do not guarantee uninterrupted service, timely notifications, a particular meal match, or continued access to every feature. Keep any records you need for care separately; Embryly is not a clinical record system.</p><p>We remain responsible for obligations the law places on us. A third party disclaimer does not excuse our own statutory duties. External links are provided for convenience and are governed by the destination’s terms and privacy practices.</p>'''),
('liability','Warranties and limits of liability', '''<p>To the extent permitted by applicable law, the Service is provided as available, without guarantees of fitness for a particular purpose, uninterrupted availability, or correctness of AI outputs. You should independently verify information before relying on it. This wording does not exclude mandatory quality, conformity, or consumer guarantees.</p><p>To the extent legally permitted, we are not liable for indirect or consequential losses, lost profits, or loss of opportunity arising from the Service. Our aggregate liability for claims arising from the Service is limited to the greater of US $50 or the amount you paid for the Service in the 12 months before the event giving rise to the claim, only where such a cap is lawful and enforceable.</p><p><strong>Nothing in these Terms excludes or limits liability for fraud, intentional misconduct, gross negligence where it cannot lawfully be limited, death or personal injury caused by negligence where protected by law, or any other liability or remedy that cannot legally be excluded.</strong> Statutory data protection compensation, consumer remedies, and nonwaivable rights remain intact. These Terms do not require you to accept risks caused by conduct for which we remain legally responsible.</p>'''),
('termination','Stopping use and account closure', '''<p>You may stop using the Service at any time. Account deactivation, permanent data erasure, and subscription cancellation are different actions. The current account closure flow offers a 30 day restoration period and does not itself guarantee permanent deletion. Contact us for a permanent erasure request under the Privacy Policy. Manage subscriptions separately with Apple.</p><p>If access is terminated, provisions reasonably needed to resolve prior obligations, protect intellectual property, or address lawful liability and disputes continue to apply. Termination does not remove refund or data protection rights.</p>'''),
('disputes','Disputes and applicable law', '''<p>The existing terms designate Illinois law and courts in Cook County, Illinois, USA. This proposed update retains that position only to the extent permitted by applicable law. If you are a consumer, the mandatory protections and courts available in your country of residence are not displaced. You may contact <a href="mailto:info@benekan.com">info@benekan.com</a> to try to resolve a concern, but doing so is not a condition on exercising a statutory right.</p><p>This draft does not add mandatory arbitration, waive class action or jury rights, or shorten statutory limitation periods. If a provision is unenforceable, the rest continues only to the extent legally permitted and consistent with the agreement’s purpose.</p>'''),
('changes','Changes and contact', '''<p>We may revise these Terms when features, law, or operations change. Material changes will be communicated with the notice and renewed acceptance required by law. Updates apply prospectively and do not retroactively remove accrued rights. The effective date will be set when the reviewed terms are published.</p><p>For legal or content concerns, write to Benekan Technologies LLC at <a href="mailto:info@benekan.com">info@benekan.com</a>. For health questions, contact your care team rather than app support.</p>''')]
legal('terms-of-use.html','Terms of service','What Embryly offers, where its limits are, and what you can expect from us.','Embryly offers general meal inspiration and AI assisted food information. It is not medical care. Outputs and illustrations can be wrong, and no validated overall accuracy percentage is established. Check actual foods and follow your care team’s advice. Your mandatory legal rights remain protected.',terms)
privacy=[
('controller','Who is responsible', '''<p>Benekan Technologies LLC, United States, operates Embryly and is the controller responsible for the personal information described here. Contact <a href="mailto:info@benekan.com">info@benekan.com</a> for privacy questions, access, correction, export, erasure, consent withdrawal, or an appeal. This notice covers the app, this website, and support communications.</p><p>This is a proposed update based on the current implementation. It does not claim GDPR certification, HIPAA certification, or regulatory approval. A privacy notice explains processing; merely reading it or using the website is not explicit consent to sensitive health processing. The separate <a href="consumer-health-privacy.html">Consumer Health Data Privacy Notice</a> addresses health information in more detail.</p>'''),
('collected','Information collected and its sources', '''<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Examples and source</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Account and authentication</td><td>Name, email, account identifier, authentication credentials or provider identifiers supplied by you or your chosen Apple/Google sign in provider.</td><td>Sign in, account access, support, and security.</td></tr><tr><td>Pregnancy and health related information</td><td>Due date, pregnancy week, journey stage, stated conditions, allergies, ingredient avoidances, goals, weight, belly measurements, water, meals, cravings, feelings, and notes you enter.</td><td>Tracking and the requested matching or contextual guidance.</td></tr><tr><td>Food scans and content</td><td>Images you capture or select, barcode values, product lookup results, saved meal photos, estimated nutrients, and AI generated analysis.</td><td>Identify food, generate information, and save food records.</td></tr><tr><td>Preferences and inferences</td><td>Dietary and cultural preferences; inferred meal matches, pregnancy week from a due date, or nutrient totals from logged meals.</td><td>Personalize suggestions. Inferences can be inaccurate and may themselves reveal health information.</td></tr><tr><td>Purchase records</td><td>App Store product, transaction, entitlement, renewal, and verification records received from Apple and our subscription service.</td><td>Verify and restore access, handle subscription support, and prevent fraud.</td></tr><tr><td>Technical and support records</td><td>IP address, request timing, device or app details where supplied, authentication and server logs, and messages you send.</td><td>Deliver the service, investigate errors, secure accounts, and respond to requests.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Apple handles payment card details for App Store purchases; our app receives transaction and entitlement data rather than your full card number. We do not need your contacts or precise location for the described features. Your photo library is not automatically imported. Only content you choose for a feature should be submitted.</p>'''),
('sensitive','Pregnancy information is sensitive', '''<p>Pregnancy dates, medical conditions, allergies, body measurements, and inferences from these records can be sensitive health data. Dietary preferences can also reveal religious beliefs or other sensitive details. General wellness positioning does not make these records nonsensitive.</p><p>Provide only information you want processed for the requested feature. Do not upload medical documents or other people’s records into a food scan. Optional details can be omitted where the feature allows; some personalization cannot function without relevant inputs. Account based features need certain information to operate, but this does not authorize unrelated uses.</p><p>The present app records wellness, privacy, and analytics acknowledgments in onboarding. A bundled acknowledgment is not, by itself, proof of valid explicit consent for every sensitive use. Where a use legally requires separate explicit consent, that permission must be obtained before that use. Contact us to withdraw consent or to request removal of sensitive information; we will explain any feature consequences and applicable retention exceptions.</p>'''),
('purposes','Purposes and legal bases', '''<p>Where the EU or UK GDPR applies, each processing purpose needs an Article 6 lawful basis, and processing special category data also needs an Article 9 condition. A contract or legitimate interest alone is not enough for health data. The relevant basis depends on the purpose and must be supported by the actual implementation.</p><ul><li><strong>Requested account and paid services:</strong> performance of our agreement, for ordinary account and entitlement data necessary to provide those services.</li><li><strong>Health based personalization and tracking:</strong> the requested service together with an applicable special category condition, ordinarily explicit consent where required. Consent must be specific, informed, and withdrawable.</li><li><strong>Security and essential diagnostics:</strong> legitimate interests in protecting the service, subject to a balancing assessment and data minimization; sensitive content needs an additional lawful condition.</li><li><strong>Legal, accounting, and rights requests:</strong> compliance with applicable legal obligations; establishment, exercise, or defense of legal claims where relevant.</li><li><strong>Optional analytics or marketing:</strong> consent where required. Core service access must not be conditioned on unnecessary optional tracking consent.</li></ul><p>You may object to processing based on legitimate interests. Withdrawal does not make earlier lawful processing unlawful. We will not treat this policy as permission to start an incompatible new use.</p>'''),
('ai-processing','What goes to AI and product lookup providers', '''<p>Food photo scans are sent through our backend to OpenAI’s API. The analysis request can contain the image and relevant profile context: pregnancy week, dietary and cultural preferences, ingredient avoidances, reported conditions, goals, food concerns, daily nutrient summaries, and recent weight information where available. This is more than an anonymous picture and may disclose sensitive health information.</p><p>Barcode scans query Open Food Facts using the barcode. Product names, ingredients, allergen tags, and nutrition returned from that service may then be sent to OpenAI with contextual information for analysis. The barcode lookup itself is not designed to send your full pregnancy profile to Open Food Facts.</p><p>OpenAI states that API data is not used to train its models by default unless the customer opts in. Its standard abuse monitoring retention can be up to 30 days, with exceptions and configuration dependent controls. We have not represented Embryly as having a zero data retention arrangement. See <a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/your-data">OpenAI’s API data controls</a>. Consumer ChatGPT settings do not control this app’s API requests.</p><p>The prepared meal catalog uses matching rules; selecting a daily catalog meal is distinct from submitting a new image for AI analysis. AI output can be inaccurate, including inferences about your food or preferences. You can correct your input, choose a different meal, or request assistance.</p>'''),
('storage','Storage, sharing, and current photo limitations', '''<p>Supabase provides authentication, databases, storage, and backend functions used by the app. OpenAI processes scan requests. Apple and, if you choose it, Google handle sign in; Apple also handles purchases. Our subscription backend verifies transactions and access. Hosting and email providers process website requests and correspondence needed to deliver those services.</p><p><strong>Current limitation:</strong> saved food photos are uploaded to the food image store using public URLs, rather than private, expiring image links. A person with a URL may be able to access the image without signing into your account. Some images may be associated with shared food records. Do not include identifiable people or sensitive documents in food photos. Contact us about removing an image. We cannot truthfully promise that current saved images are accessible only to you.</p><p>Operational logs can currently include profile context, nutrient or weight summaries, and scan results. Access by authorized staff and infrastructure providers may be needed for support and diagnostics. This is not an invitation to submit extra sensitive data; our release review identifies minimization and retention controls that need verification.</p><p>We do not sell personal information or use it for cross context behavioral advertising in the described service. We may disclose information to meet a lawful obligation, respond to valid legal process, protect against misuse, or complete a business transfer subject to applicable safeguards. This is not a promise that health information is immune from every lawful request. A new disclosure requiring consent will require that consent.</p>'''),
('retention','Retention, deactivation, and permanent erasure', '''<p>Account and tracking records remain available while an account is active, subject to the purposes above. A universal fixed retention period for every database, backup, log, and provider has not been verified. Retention must be limited to what is needed for service delivery, lawful records, security, disputes, and applicable rights. We do not promise instant removal from every backup or provider.</p><p><strong>The current in app account deletion flow deactivates the account and allows restoration for 30 days. It does not automatically permanently erase the underlying data when that window ends.</strong> For permanent erasure, contact <a href="mailto:info@benekan.com?subject=Embryly%20permanent%20erasure%20request">info@benekan.com</a>. We will verify the request proportionately and explain completion, any legal exception, or a lawful extension. A support request can also cover uploaded images and derived records.</p><p>Transaction records or narrowly limited information may need to be retained for tax, fraud prevention, legal obligations, or claims. Backup copies may persist until the relevant rotation cycle; they must not be restored to active use inconsistently with a valid erasure request. Deactivation does not cancel an App Store subscription. Erasing an app from your phone does not itself remove cloud records.</p>'''),
('controls','Your controls and privacy requests', '''<ul><li>Review and change editable preferences and profile information in the app. Future recommendations use the saved settings.</li><li>Revoke camera, selected photo, or notification permissions in your device settings. Revocation stops future access but does not erase information already uploaded.</li><li>Contact us for access, correction, a portable copy, deletion, restriction, an objection, or consent withdrawal. There is no verified self service data export feature, so please use the support contact.</li><li>Use the email associated with your account and specify the right you want to exercise. Do not send identity documents unless we explain why additional verification is necessary and provide an appropriate method.</li></ul><p>Where GDPR applies, we generally respond within one month and may extend by up to two further months for complex or numerous requests with the required notice. Other applicable laws have their own deadlines. Requests are generally free; any permitted fee or refusal will be explained. We do not penalize you for exercising a protected right, although removing necessary data can limit a related feature.</p><p>EU/EEA residents may complain to their local supervisory authority; UK residents may contact the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">Information Commissioner’s Office</a>. You do not need to contact us first to exercise a regulatory complaint right.</p>'''),
('states','United States and consumer health rights', '''<p>Where applicable, state laws may provide rights to know, access, correct, delete, obtain a copy, appeal a refusal, limit certain sensitive processing, or opt out of sale, targeted advertising, and specified profiling. These rights depend on the law’s scope and exceptions; we do not assume every statute applies identically to every user.</p><p>We do not sell health data or use it for targeted advertising in the described service. We do not operate healthcare location geofencing. Washington and other applicable consumer health privacy protections may reach information outside HIPAA. See our distinct <a href="consumer-health-privacy.html">Consumer Health Data Privacy Notice</a>, linked from the home page footer, for categories, sources, sharing, rights, and appeals.</p><p>Embryly is a consumer wellness service, not presented as your healthcare provider’s HIPAA covered medical record system. That does not remove obligations under consumer protection, breach notification, or other privacy laws. We will make legally required notifications if a reportable incident occurs; the applicable rule and facts determine the required recipients and timing.</p>'''),
('international','International transfers', '''<p>Benekan Technologies LLC is based in the United States. Information may be processed in the United States and other locations used by our providers. The production database region, complete processor list, backup locations, and transfer arrangements must be confirmed before an international launch claim is made.</p><p>Where GDPR or UK GDPR restricts a transfer, a valid mechanism is required, such as an applicable adequacy decision or properly implemented standard contractual clauses and additional safeguards where needed. This notice does not itself establish such a mechanism or claim that every provider arrangement has been verified. Contact us for information about the arrangements relevant to your data. No EU or UK representative or data protection officer is named in this draft without a confirmed appointment.</p>'''),
('automation','Personalization and automated decisions', '''<p>Embryly uses software to infer a pregnancy week from supplied dates, rank meal ideas, estimate nutrients, and produce scan information. These outputs can influence what you see, but they are not used by Embryly to make lending, employment, insurance, healthcare eligibility, or other similarly significant legal decisions about you.</p><p>Do not use the app as the sole basis for a medical decision. Where applicable law gives rights regarding significant automated decisions, those rights are preserved. You may contact us to question an output or correct the information used. A food ranking or score is not a clinical assessment.</p>'''),
('website','Website cookies, analytics, and contact', '''<p>This redesigned website does not install advertising pixels or optional analytics scripts and does not use cookies or browser storage for advertising. Its fonts and product images are served as site assets. The hosting provider may still process ordinary request information, including your IP address, to deliver and secure pages. Visiting an external link exposes information to that destination under its own policy.</p><p>The contact form prepares a message in your email app. It does not submit the form to a website database. The message is transmitted when you send it using your email provider. We then process the correspondence to answer your request. Do not include medical documents or passwords. Optional tracking, if introduced later, requires an updated notice and consent controls where the law requires them.</p><p>The current app contains an analytics acknowledgment, but no active third party product analytics integration was established by this code review. Essential operational logs are separate from optional analytics. We do not treat a Do Not Track signal as a substitute for legally required opt out mechanisms. Global Privacy Control must be honored where applicable to a covered activity.</p>'''),
('security','Security and incident handling', '''<p>We use account authentication and HTTPS connections for the described services. Security depends on the application, access policies, provider configuration, and staff procedures, and no system can guarantee absolute security. The public image URL and logging limitations above are material exceptions to any broad “only you can access your information” statement.</p><p>Report a suspected privacy or security issue to <a href="mailto:info@benekan.com?subject=Embryly%20privacy%20or%20security%20issue">info@benekan.com</a>. Include only the information necessary to explain the issue. We will investigate and take actions and notifications required by applicable law. The website does not offer an emergency response service.</p>'''),
('children','Age limits and changes', '''<p>Embryly is intended for adults aged 18 or older. If you believe a child’s information was submitted, contact us so we can investigate and take appropriate action. An age statement alone is not a substitute for effective safeguards.</p><p>We will update this notice when practices change and provide material notices or obtain new consent where required. Continued use is not automatically consent to a new sensitive purpose. The final effective date and verified company contact details will be confirmed before publication. Questions may be sent to Benekan Technologies LLC at <a href="mailto:info@benekan.com">info@benekan.com</a>.</p>''')]
legal('privacy-policy.html','Privacy policy','What you share, how the app uses it, and how to exercise your choices.','Pregnancy information is sensitive. Embryly uses Supabase for cloud services and OpenAI for scan analysis, which can include pregnancy and profile context. Current saved food photos use public URLs, and account deactivation is not permanent erasure. Contact info@benekan.com for privacy requests. We do not present this draft as proof of GDPR compliance.',privacy)
health=[
('scope','Scope and contact','''<p>This notice supplements the <a href="privacy-policy.html">Privacy Policy</a> for consumer health data handled by Benekan Technologies LLC through Embryly. It is intended to explain practices relevant to Washington’s My Health My Data Act and other applicable consumer health laws, without claiming that wording alone establishes compliance. Contact <a href="mailto:info@benekan.com">info@benekan.com</a> for a health data request.</p>'''),
('categories','Health data categories and sources','''<p>We collect information you supply about pregnancy, due dates, pregnancy stage, health conditions, allergies, dietary avoidances, weight, belly measurements, water intake, meals, cravings, feelings, food concerns, and goals. Images, scan results, and food journal entries can also reveal health information. We derive pregnancy week, nutrient summaries, meal matches, and AI generated food assessments from those inputs.</p><p>The sources are you, your app activity, the food content or barcodes you submit, product information returned by Open Food Facts, and the inferences generated by our software or AI service. Authentication and account identifiers connect records to an account. We do not need precise location data and do not use geofencing around healthcare facilities.</p>'''),
('use','Why data is collected and used','''<p>The purposes are to deliver requested tracking, match general meal ideas, contextualize scans, maintain records, answer support and rights requests, and secure the service. Health data is not used to decide insurance, employment, credit, or eligibility for healthcare. We do not sell health data or use it for targeted advertising in the described service.</p><p>Collection and sharing must have any permission or other basis required by applicable law. A broad acceptance of terms does not automatically authorize a new health data use. Where a separate opt in is required, it must be obtained before the relevant processing; the existing bundled onboarding acknowledgments need review against those requirements.</p>'''),
('recipients','Who can receive it','''<p>Supabase receives account, tracking, storage, and backend data necessary for the app. OpenAI receives submitted food images and relevant health and preference context for scan analysis. Authorized support and technical providers can process information needed for their function, including operational records. Apple handles purchase data; a chosen sign in provider supplies authentication data. We may disclose limited information where legally required or in a lawful business transfer, subject to applicable protections.</p><p>Saved food images currently use public URLs and may be associated with shared food records. Anyone with such a URL may be able to retrieve an image without an account. Operational logs may contain sensitive context. These limitations are described in the main Privacy Policy and must not be mistaken for confidential clinical storage. We do not list an undisclosed affiliate as an authorized health data recipient.</p>'''),
('rights','Access, withdrawal, deletion, and appeals','''<p>Where applicable, you can ask whether we collect or share your consumer health data, request access and a list of relevant recipients as the law provides, withdraw consent, or request deletion. Email <a href="mailto:info@benekan.com?subject=Embryly%20consumer%20health%20data%20request">info@benekan.com</a> from the address associated with your account. We may reasonably verify identity and will follow applicable deadlines, exceptions, and processor notification duties.</p><p>If we deny a request, you may appeal by replying with “Privacy appeal” and explaining the issue. We will explain the result within the applicable legal timeframe and provide the relevant complaint route. Washington residents can contact the <a href="https://www.atg.wa.gov/file-complaint">Washington Attorney General</a>. This does not limit other remedies.</p><p>The current account deactivation feature offers restoration for 30 days but does not perform automatic permanent erasure. Use the support route for a permanent deletion request; applicable rights are not limited by the account button’s behavior. Withdrawing necessary information may stop related personalized features. We will not discriminate against you for exercising protected rights.</p>''')]
legal('consumer-health-privacy.html','Consumer health data privacy','A separate notice for pregnancy and other health related information.','This notice identifies health data categories, purposes, recipients, and request routes. Current public photo URLs and account deactivation limitations are material. Permanent erasure and other rights can be requested at info@benekan.com.',health)
sources=[
('accuracy','What accuracy means here','''<p><strong>Validated overall accuracy: not established. No percentage is available.</strong> We have not identified an independent evaluation supporting a single accuracy percentage across food identification, ingredient detection, nutrient estimation, pregnancy suitability, and baby artwork. Those are different tasks and would require different tests. A confidence score is not the chance that a meal is safe for a particular person.</p><p>The existing app contains legacy “up to 90% accuracy” wording. This preview does not repeat it as a performance claim. It should be removed or supported by a clearly scoped, reproducible evaluation before use. No clinical approval or kitchen testing is implied by an automated editorial check.</p>'''),
('references','The references in our catalog','''<p>These public resources appear in the app’s catalog source records or editorial publication notes. They supply background guidance or reference data; the organizations have not endorsed Embryly.</p><ul><li><a href="https://www.cdc.gov/food-safety/foods/pregnant-women.html">CDC: Safer Food Choices for Pregnant Women</a> — general food selection and handling guidance.</li><li><a href="https://www.foodsafety.gov/people-at-risk/pregnant-women">FoodSafety.gov: People at Risk, Pregnant Women</a> — pregnancy food safety considerations.</li><li><a href="https://www.foodsafety.gov/food-safety-charts/safe-minimum-internal-temperatures">FoodSafety.gov: Safe Minimum Internal Temperatures</a> — cooking and reheating reference temperatures.</li><li><a href="https://www.fda.gov/food/consumers/advice-about-eating-fish">FDA/EPA: Advice About Eating Fish</a> — fish choices and frequency guidance.</li><li><a href="https://www.nhs.uk/pregnancy/keeping-well/have-a-healthy-diet/">NHS: Have a healthy diet in pregnancy</a> — general dietary variety guidance.</li><li><a href="https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/">USDA FoodData Central</a> and <a href="https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/download-datasets/">SR Legacy data</a> — reference ingredient nutrients. AI selected ingredient matches and recipe sums introduce uncertainty.</li><li><a href="https://world.openfoodfacts.org/">Open Food Facts</a> — community maintained barcode, ingredient, allergen, and nutrition records. This is product data, not clinical advice.</li></ul><p>Links checked September 26, 2026. Country specific advice can differ. Check the original source and your local care team rather than assuming every rule is universal.</p>'''),
('method','How content reaches your screen','''<p>The starting catalog combines prepared meal records, generated imagery, ingredient tags, recipes, and estimated nutrient data. The current publication records describe an automated editorial review, not independent medical review. The selection rules filter and rank matching records using pregnancy week, saved preferences, and recent meal history.</p><p>Food scans use an AI model and, for barcodes, product lookup data. They are not guaranteed to consult these reference pages during each response. Nutrition estimates are not laboratory measurements. Recommendations do not establish a complete daily nutrient intake or a prescribed diet.</p>'''),
('visuals','About the baby and meal visuals','''<p>Baby images for weeks 1 through 42 are artistic, AI assisted illustrations. They are not clinical reference plates, personalized scans, or verified depictions of exact development in a particular week. They cannot date a pregnancy or assess a baby’s growth, anatomy, viability, or wellbeing. A clinician’s measurements and examinations are the appropriate basis for those questions.</p><p>Meal imagery is illustrative and can differ from actual ingredients, portions, or cooking results. Marketing screenshots display real app screens with fictional sample records. They are product demonstrations, not patient outcomes. No visual is evidence that a particular food is safe.</p>'''),
('corrections','Questions and corrections','''<p>If a meal, image, source, or scan appears wrong, <a href="contact.html">report it to us</a>. Describe the content and the correction you believe is needed without sending unnecessary personal health information. Check the original label or source and seek a professional opinion if the issue affects a decision about your health.</p><p>For personal medical questions or suspected illness, contact your care team. Our support channel is for product and content issues, not clinical assessment.</p>''')]
legal('sources.html','Sources & accuracy','A clearer view of where our information comes from and what it can tell you.','Embryly combines public reference guidance, prepared meal records, matching rules, and AI generated information. Source citations are not medical approval. No independently validated overall accuracy percentage is established.',sources)
def article(path,title,deck,category,cover,body,minutes):
 schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@graph':[{'@type':'BlogPosting','headline':title,'description':deck,'author':{'@type':'Organization','name':'Embryly Editorial Team'},'publisher':{'@type':'Organization','name':'Embryly'},'datePublished':DATE,'dateModified':DATE,'mainEntityOfPage':DOMAIN+'/'+path,'image':DOMAIN+'/assets/'+cover},{'@type':'BreadcrumbList','itemListElement':[{'@type':'ListItem','position':1,'name':'Home','item':DOMAIN+'/index.html'},{'@type':'ListItem','position':2,'name':'Journal','item':DOMAIN+'/blog/index.html'},{'@type':'ListItem','position':3,'name':title,'item':DOMAIN+'/'+path}]}]}
 page(path,title,deck,f'''<article class="article"><header class="article-header"><a class="text-link" href="index.html">← The Embryly journal</a><div class="meta" style="margin-top:35px">{category.upper()} · {minutes} MIN READ</div><h1>{title}</h1><p class="article-deck">{deck}</p><p class="meta">Embryly Editorial Team · September 26, 2026</p></header><div class="article-body">{body}</div></article>''',prefix='../',schema=schema)
food='''<p><strong>During pregnancy, food safety is about the food, its preparation, and how it has been stored.</strong> A name or photograph cannot tell the whole story. Start with the label, choose properly prepared ingredients, use a thermometer when cooking, and ask your care team about your own circumstances. This guide uses US food safety recommendations; local advice may differ.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="../index.html#download">Explore Embryly ↗</a><br>Embryly helps organize food ideas and questions. It cannot certify that a meal is safe.</p><figure style="margin:0"><div class="article-cover"><img src="../assets/chicken-plate.png" width="1280" height="1280" alt="Illustrative chicken plate with vegetables"></div><figcaption>Illustrative catalog artwork. An image cannot verify cooking temperature.</figcaption></figure><h2>Ask a more useful question.</h2><p>“Can I eat cheese?” is a start, but “Is this cheese pasteurized, and does this type need heating?” gives you something you can check. The same is true for a sandwich, a salad, or a bowl of leftovers. Try breaking the decision into three parts: what is in it, what has happened to it, and what you can verify now.</p><p>This is especially useful when you are eating somewhere unfamiliar. You do not have to identify every detail from a picture. Ask the person preparing the meal about ingredients and cooking, look at the package if there is one, and choose another option if an important answer is unavailable.</p><h2>Four checks before you eat.</h2><h3>1. Read the label, not just the front.</h3><p>Check the actual ingredients and allergen statements, even if you have bought the product before. Formulations and packaging change. Look for pasteurization information on dairy and juice. The <a href="https://www.cdc.gov/food-safety/foods/pregnant-women.html">CDC’s pregnancy food guide</a> also identifies special precautions for fresh queso fresco type cheeses and deli sliced cheese; “made with pasteurized milk” is not a universal all clear for every food.</p><h3>2. Check how it was cooked.</h3><p>Use a food thermometer rather than a photo, a browned surface, or a guess. <a href="https://www.foodsafety.gov/food-safety-charts/safe-minimum-internal-temperatures">US minimum temperature guidance</a> lists 165°F (74°C) for poultry and leftovers, 160°F (71°C) for ground beef, pork, veal, or lamb, and 145°F (63°C) plus a three minute rest for whole cuts of those meats. Fish is generally cooked to 145°F (63°C). Different foods require different checks.</p><h3>3. Remember what you cannot see.</h3><p>A freshly made dish can still contain an ingredient that needs extra care. <a href="https://www.foodsafety.gov/people-at-risk/pregnant-women">FoodSafety.gov</a> advises avoiding raw sprouts, unpasteurized milk, and raw or undercooked seafood in pregnancy. It advises reheating deli meats until steaming hot or 165°F (74°C). Refrigerated smoked seafood needs special handling, such as being thoroughly cooked in a dish. Read the full guidance for the specific food rather than using a blanket rule for an entire cuisine.</p><h3>4. Include storage in the decision.</h3><p>Think about the trip home, the time on the counter, and whether food has been kept chilled. The <a href="https://www.cdc.gov/food-safety/prevention/index.html">CDC’s prevention guidance</a> explains cleaning, separating raw foods, cooking, and chilling. If you do not know a food’s storage history, an app cannot reconstruct it. A pleasing smell or appearance is not a substitute for safe handling.</p><h2>Fish is not a simple yes or no.</h2><p>The <a href="https://www.fda.gov/food/consumers/advice-about-eating-fish">FDA and EPA fish chart</a> distinguishes species by mercury level. Their US guidance recommends two to three servings a week from the “Best Choices” category for people who are pregnant or breastfeeding. Preparation still matters: a lower mercury fish served raw is not the same choice as that fish properly cooked. Follow local advisories for fish you catch and discuss individual needs with your care team.</p><h2>Where a food scan can help.</h2><p>A scan can be a starting point for identifying a dish or reading product information. It can also be wrong. Hidden ingredients, a changed recipe, an unclear photograph, or an outdated barcode entry can change the answer. A model cannot test for bacteria, measure a cooking temperature, or confirm an allergen free kitchen.</p><p>Embryly offers general AI assisted food information, not a safety certification. There is no independently validated overall accuracy percentage for its outputs. Use a result to help you form a question, then verify the relevant detail. Our <a href="../sources.html">sources and accuracy page</a> explains the distinction.</p><h2>A calmer way forward.</h2><p>You do not need to turn every meal into an investigation. Build a few familiar choices around ingredients and preparation you understand. Keep a short list of questions for your next appointment, and ask for guidance suited to your allergies, conditions, and local food rules. If you suspect foodborne illness or feel unwell during pregnancy, contact your care team promptly rather than asking an app to assess the symptoms.</p><p>For the planning side of everyday eating, read <a href="pregnancy-meal-planning.html">our guide to a flexible pregnancy meal plan</a>.</p><div class="callout"><p><strong>About this article</strong><br>Educational content by the Embryly Editorial Team, not individually tailored advice or a clinician reviewed treatment plan. Reference links checked September 26, 2026.</p></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul class="source-list"><li><a href="https://www.cdc.gov/food-safety/foods/pregnant-women.html">CDC: Safer Food Choices for Pregnant Women</a></li><li><a href="https://www.foodsafety.gov/people-at-risk/pregnant-women">FoodSafety.gov: Pregnancy food safety</a></li><li><a href="https://www.foodsafety.gov/food-safety-charts/safe-minimum-internal-temperatures">FoodSafety.gov: Safe minimum temperatures</a></li><li><a href="https://www.cdc.gov/food-safety/prevention/index.html">CDC: Preventing food poisoning</a></li><li><a href="https://www.fda.gov/food/consumers/advice-about-eating-fish">FDA/EPA: Advice about eating fish</a></li></ul>'''
article('blog/pregnancy-food-safety.html','Can I eat this? A calmer guide to food safety in pregnancy.','A practical starting point for checking ingredients, preparation, and storage without expecting a photo to tell the whole story.','Food safety','chicken-plate.png',food,6)
meals='''<p><strong>A useful pregnancy meal plan gives you options, not another standard to live up to.</strong> Start with a few familiar breakfasts, lunches, and dinners, vary ingredients over the week, and leave room to change your mind. Your clinician or dietitian should guide any specific nutritional needs, supplements, or restrictions; a general meal app does not replace that plan.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="../index.html#download">Explore Embryly ↗</a><br>Embryly matches meal ideas to your saved preferences and pregnancy week, so there is a place to start.</p><figure style="margin:0"><div class="article-cover" style="background:#e1e3d8"><img src="../assets/chickpea-plate.png" width="1280" height="1280" alt="Illustrative chickpea and avocado meal"></div><figcaption>Illustrative meal artwork from the Embryly catalog. Ingredients and portions need separate checks.</figcaption></figure><h2>Plan around variety, not a perfect day.</h2><p>The <a href="https://www.nhs.uk/pregnancy/keeping-well/have-a-healthy-diet/">NHS pregnancy nutrition guide</a> encourages a variety of foods rather than a special restrictive diet, and says balance can be considered over a week rather than achieved at every meal. It also explains that supplements remain important; food ideas are not a replacement for prescribed or recommended supplements.</p><p>For planning, give yourself a small pool of choices. Two or three breakfasts, a few lunches, and several dinners can be easier to use than a rigid seven day schedule. That is an organizing method, not a prescribed portion count or an instruction about how often you should eat.</p><h2>Build a short list for each part of the day.</h2><h3>Breakfast: make the first decision smaller.</h3><p>You might keep oats, a pasteurized yogurt option, or thoroughly cooked eggs in your list if they fit your needs. Add ingredients you enjoy and can tolerate. A familiar option is useful on a rushed morning. The purpose is to reduce the decision, not to prove that one breakfast meets every nutritional requirement.</p><h3>Lunch: choose something practical.</h3><p>A freshly prepared bean and grain bowl, a cooked vegetable dish, or a safely reheated meal can be a starting point. Consider where you will eat and whether you have refrigeration or reheating available. Keep ingredients you avoid out of the plan, and do not assume a similar looking store bought dish uses the same recipe.</p><h3>Dinner: change one element at a time.</h3><p>If you like a particular meal format, try a different vegetable, protein, or grain rather than learning an entirely new recipe every evening. Check the preparation instructions each time, especially if swapping a plant ingredient for poultry or fish. The new ingredient may need a different cooking process.</p><h2>Keep safety part of the routine.</h2><p>Planning ahead only helps if food is handled appropriately. Follow <a href="https://www.cdc.gov/food-safety/prevention/index.html">CDC guidance on cleaning, separating, cooking, and chilling</a>. Labeling a container with the date you made it can help you remember its history; it does not extend its storage life. Check official storage guidance for the actual dish.</p><p>US guidance recommends eggs cooked until whites and yolks are firm and pasteurized milk products, while other foods need their own checks. The <a href="https://www.cdc.gov/food-safety/foods/pregnant-women.html">CDC pregnancy food table</a> is a helpful reference. Local rules can differ, so follow your care team and the public health guidance where you live.</p><h2>Let preferences change.</h2><p>A food you enjoyed last week may be less appealing today. In Embryly, updated profile preferences inform future catalog matches. You can use that flexibility without treating a recommendation as a medical instruction. A setting for lower carbohydrate choices ranks relative options; it does not prescribe a carbohydrate target. Halal or kosher preferences do not certify sourcing or preparation.</p><p>For allergies, read the actual package and ask about cross contact. For gestational diabetes, anemia, celiac disease, or other conditions, ask a qualified professional for an individualized plan. A filter can exclude known tags, but it cannot establish that a recipe or commercial product meets your clinical needs.</p><h2>Use the plan as a starting point.</h2><p>Open a meal idea, check the ingredient list, and consider what works for your day. Choose among the options rather than assuming you should eat every recommendation. Estimated nutrients are not a complete record of your intake, and displayed meals are not guaranteed to cover all your daily requirements.</p>'''+f'''<figure><div class="article-shot">{phone('05-breakfast-recommendations','Actual Embryly breakfast recommendations showing sample catalog meals',prefix='../')}</div><figcaption>Actual Embryly screen with sample recommendations. Nutritional estimates are not a prescribed daily diet.</figcaption></figure>'''+'''<p>It is also fine to make a note of what did not work. Perhaps a dish required more preparation than you had time for, or an ingredient was difficult to find. Those observations are useful for your next shopping list. If persistent nausea, vomiting, or difficulty eating or drinking is affecting your intake, contact your care team instead of trying to solve it through meal selection alone.</p><p>For the “is this safe?” part of the decision, read <a href="pregnancy-food-safety.html">our pregnancy food safety guide</a>. For how the app’s matching works, visit <a href="../sources.html">Sources & Accuracy</a>.</p><div class="callout"><p><strong>A note on individual needs</strong><br>This is an organizational approach to general meal inspiration, not a medical diet or supplement plan. Embryly Editorial Team; references checked September 26, 2026. No clinical review is claimed.</p></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul class="source-list"><li><a href="https://www.nhs.uk/pregnancy/keeping-well/have-a-healthy-diet/">NHS: Have a healthy diet in pregnancy</a></li><li><a href="https://www.cdc.gov/food-safety/foods/pregnant-women.html">CDC: Safer food choices during pregnancy</a></li><li><a href="https://www.cdc.gov/food-safety/prevention/index.html">CDC: Preventing food poisoning</a></li><li><a href="../sources.html">Embryly’s source and implementation notes</a></li></ul>'''
article('blog/pregnancy-meal-planning.html','A pregnancy meal plan with room for real life.','A flexible way to think about breakfast, lunch, and dinner when your appetite, routine, and preferences keep changing.','Everyday nutrition','chickpea-plate.png',meals,5)
